# Truth: the two-valued logic the surface checker reasons in, true and false. A truth value is the result of a
# decidable test, and the connectives (and, or, not, implies) combine them. The deeper logic of the kernel is
# constructive and proof-relevant (a proof is a term, not just a bit), but at the surface, decidable propositions
# collapse to this boolean. The form carries a boolean value.
form truth
  link value, like boolean
